{"duration_api_ms":28450,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"827dd1a9-7865-4001-8455-8c649fd9adfe","total_cost_usd":2.5323610000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":308429,"cache_read_input_tokens":7565,"output_tokens":3170,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1082},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":308429,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":819,"cache_read_input_tokens":7565,"cache_creation_input_tokens":272127,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":272127},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":3170,"cacheReadInputTokens":7565,"cacheCreationInputTokens":308429,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.5323610000000003,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1082,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote the labels to `coder-1.json` and coded Blanca Pacheco at **rung 2, \"Forbid rules that require schools to tell parents.\"**\n\n**What the chair rests on:** her Aye vote on AB 1955 (2023-2024). This was the Assembly's 2024-06-27 vote to concur in Senate amendments, which passed 61-16. Both pages of that record are in `rests_on`:\n- **Vote page:** shows her name (`Muratsuchi, Ortega, Pacheco, Papan`) and the count (`Result: PASS, 61-16`).\n- **Chaptered bill text:** Section 220.5(a) says school entities \"shall not enact or enforce any policy, rule, or administrative regulation that would require an employee or a contractor to disclose\" a pupil's gender identity without the pupil's consent.\n\n**Why rung 2 and not a neighbouring rung:**\n- **Not rung 1** (\"Require staff to keep a student's gender identity from parents\"). Section 220.3 says staff \"shall not be required to disclose\", which permits silence but doesn't order it.\n- **Not rungs 3–5.** The bill requires no notification of parents in any form.\n- **Not preemption (H12).** The bill does stop school districts from making their own rule, but rung 2 is itself about forbidding such rules, so the passage counts as `on-question`.\n- **Single-subject.** I treated the bill as single-subject: the parent-resources and anti-retaliation sections all concern LGBTQ pupils' rights.\n- **Not near-unanimous.** 16 of 79 voted No, about 20%.\n- **In-term.** The vote falls inside her current term, which began 2022-12-05.\n\nThere are no quotes in her own words in the sources, so `quotes` is empty, and `needs_source` is empty.\n\n**One thing for review:** the bill text notes that the Assembly's 2024-04-25 floor vote was on a different, earlier version (\"Pupil health: school-based health services\"). I relied only on the concurrence vote, which was on the chaptered text.\n\nSeparately, several claude.ai connectors (Benevity, Candid, Canva, Figma, Givebutter, Harvey, WorkOS) and the Supabase plugin need authorizing, and the GitHub plugin failed to connect. None of them were needed for this task.","ttft_ms":9894,"type":"result","duration_ms":31659,"uuid":"c46ff258-f103-44c0-abd5-731428df8c1a","ttft_stream_ms":920,"time_to_request_ms":277,"first_content_frame_ms":921,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
